HOW legacy_default is computed or that it is clone-invariant.","Plan's convergence rationale is scoped to the project SET: 'A store-owned project set removes that failure mode by construction and leaves no per-repo list to disagree' — legacy_default is a per-store default, not part of that set-ownership argument.","The seed unit derives legacy_default from each clone's local jira.project config (per-clone value), so byte-identical seeds across clones are not guaranteed when configs differ, breaking the ff-only convergence the seed relies on."],"finding":"The plan's store-ownership convergence guarantee covers only the project SET, not the seeded legacy_default value; two clones with divergent jira.project config that seed before either commits to the shared tickets-branch base can write byte-divergent projects.json and fork the ff-only branch — the cross-clone disagreement the plan claims to eliminate 'by construction'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f110a0cbd622ec6da","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'seeded by an idempotent check-then-act ensure unit'; and the store-ownership paragraph ('removes that failure mode by construction and leaves no per-repo list to disagree')","norm_id":"n2c43dbc97ff4c039","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two repos/clones back one shared store but each has a different [jira] project configured; both run init/seed before the shared base carries projects.json.","A clone with jira.project unset seeds an empty legacy_default while a sibling clone with jira.project set seeds a non-empty one."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify that the seed's legacy_default is either (a) a fixed clone-invariant value, or (b) written by exactly one authority (first clone whose commit reaches the shared base wins, later clones tree-check to ok), and note that clones with divergent local jira.project must not each write a differing legacy_default; add a test asserting two clo